    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456-a1">

                <pb facs="0477" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg457"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <head>The Gorogio to Mr. Pruyn</head>
                <p>We have to state to your excellency that, at present, the former opinion of our
                    government having changed, it is desirable that the letter which Ogasawara
                    Dsusio-no-kami recently, when in office, addressed to you in relation to the
                    closing of the ports, be soon returned.</p>
                <p>Which we have to state, with respect and esteem.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian japanese-nengō"
                            when="1863-11-11">The 1st day of the 10th month of the 3d year of
                            Bunkiu, (November 11, 1863</date>.)</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MIDSUMO-IDSUMI-NO-KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>ITAKURA-SUWO-NO-KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>INOWUYE-KAWATSI-NO-KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>ARIMA-TOTAMI-NO-KAMI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States of America,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
